# Official arXiv:2607.11391v1 symmetric QW FMA (Algorithm 3 / Appendix B.1).
#
# Contract being audited:
#   1. both explicit FastTwoSum gates must satisfy FPANVerifier's exponent-order
#      precondition for all precisions;
#   2. the final (z2,z3) pair is non-overlapping;
#   3. the leading (z0,z1) non-overlap claim is EXPECTED TO BE REFUTED, exactly
#      as stated in Sec. 2.9.5 of the paper.
#
# Plain rounded adds/multiplies are represented by TwoSum/TwoProd with discarded
# residual wires, matching the paper's fma_ref.c <-> .fpan translation rule.

variable x0
variable x1
variable x2
variable x3
variable y0
variable y1
variable y2
variable y3
variable c0
variable c1
variable c2
variable c3

assume x0 strongly_dominates x1
assume x1 strongly_dominates x2
assume x2 strongly_dominates x3
assume y0 strongly_dominates y1
assume y1 strongly_dominates y2
assume y2 strongly_dominates y3
assume c0 strongly_dominates c1
assume c1 strongly_dominates c2
assume c2 strongly_dominates c3

variable p00
variable e00
variable p01
variable e01
variable p10
variable e10
variable p02
variable e02
variable p11
variable e11
variable p20
variable e20
variable p03
variable e03
variable p12
variable e12
variable p21
variable e21
variable p30
variable e30

two_prod x0 y0 p00 e00
two_prod x0 y1 p01 e01
two_prod x1 y0 p10 e10
two_prod x0 y2 p02 e02
two_prod x1 y1 p11 e11
two_prod x2 y0 p20 e20
# Plain i+j=3 products: residuals intentionally discarded.
two_prod x0 y3 p03 e03
two_prod x1 y2 p12 e12
two_prod x2 y1 p21 e21
two_prod x3 y0 p30 e30

# D = (P03 + P30) + (P12 + P21).
two_sum p03 p30
two_sum p12 p21
two_sum p03 p12

# (B,r) = TwoSum(P00,c0).
two_sum p00 c0

# A1 and f1..f4.
two_sum p01 p10
two_sum p01 e00
two_sum p01 c1
two_sum p01 c0

# A2 and g1..g9; E01/E10 are paired first for x<->y symmetry.
two_sum p02 p20
two_sum p02 p11
two_sum e01 e10
two_sum p02 e01
two_sum p02 c2
two_sum p02 p10
two_sum p02 e00
two_sum p02 c1
two_sum p02 c0

# A3 rounded-add tree from Appendix B.1.
two_sum e02 e20
two_sum e11 p03
two_sum e02 e11
two_sum e02 c3

two_sum p20 p11
two_sum e01 e10
two_sum p20 e01
two_sum p10 e00
two_sum c1 c0
two_sum p10 c1
two_sum p20 p10
two_sum p20 c2
two_sum e02 p20

# Algorithm 3 renormalization: F T T / T T F.
# Live tuple is (p00,p01,p02,e02) = (B,A1,A2,A3).
fast_two_sum p00 p01
two_sum      p01 p02
two_sum      p02 e02

two_sum      p00 p01
two_sum      p01 p02
fast_two_sum p02 e02

# Paper Sec. 2.9.5: this weak leading non-overlap claim is refuted.
prove p00 s_dominates p01

# The final FastTwoSum pair should retain a strong non-overlap relation.
prove p02 strongly_dominates e02
